ere  the economic hit was absolutely massive  for example Alsace produced more cotton  textiles than the entirety of Germany  combined in 1871 and it now being cut  off from France meant that they had no  more customers and that German textiles  now faced tremendous competition this  competition to German textiles were so  bad it was proposed that in order to  mitigate this Alsace be given to  Switzerland instead but shockingly the  Kaiser said no so after 40 years was the  region fully integrated not really  whilst the region had gained some  autonomy over the years its people  wanted more in 1913 German soldiers  insulted the local population using the  term vac as a derogatory term for the  people of Alsace Lorraine iam what's  called there's a Bern incident this led  to protests and the kaiser wilhelm ii  subsequently sided with the soldiers  which basically destroyed any loyalty  the region had to the empire when the  first world  war broke out a year later sympathies  for France remained high as such army  conscripts from Alsace Lorraine was sent  to the Eastern Front so that the divided  loyalties wouldn't be tested furthermore  speaking French in public was banned and  the people of the region were treated  poorly since the government was worried  about pro-french spies and ultimately  after French victory in the First World  War the region was returned to France  and the issue over who owned it was  totally settled forever I hope you  enjoyed this episode and thank you for  watching and a special thanks to all of  these patrons you see on screen for  their generosity in supporting the show  and a particularly special thanks to  James Bissonnette party-boy Co kazarka  flash Rob Waterhouse Chris wicker  Michael Reynolds Thomas McGill Gustav  Swan Winston Hayward Skye Chappell the  amusement park Ives Adam Harvey  and lastly rafail
 

